[{:db/id "q-77008/selection/38435e9068e2fe59fa48a90055807820180c60c7327253df92ca359a244f7202" :answer/id #uuid "17c17ee5-e87e-5d33-bfd3-5f9e8b91d0db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77008/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4b97a787-a1f0-54f9-8bad-14b138fe3430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77008/selection/25896a72f5d013c50bb7cb627bf4b333dd1dedb6f0f4e897db2f1ea33bb9ec65" :answer/id #uuid "09fe2727-a04c-5f16-b597-7e39f4e3b962" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi -2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77008/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "b4aacb1a-8ca5-547f-9995-cf3baa6e0fd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77008/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "f471322e-f88e-5279-987d-5a0721866964" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77008/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "54a45544-c0aa-50c0-90ce-418e9cc6f417" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77008/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-77008/selection/38435e9068e2fe59fa48a90055807820180c60c7327253df92ca359a244f7202" "q-77008/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-77008/selection/25896a72f5d013c50bb7cb627bf4b333dd1dedb6f0f4e897db2f1ea33bb9ec65" "q-77008/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-77008/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77008" :question/id #uuid "86093429-bf79-5738-9f65-4a1d67949670" :question/math-academy-id "q-77008" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/assets/dea7eed9213ddf1bb3293950e2490b120a061e9add1172d3b850ccbc58f90454.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(y+x)\\,i+x\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4$ traversed from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $B(0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Notice that we can write its equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, our curve is a part-ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $2$ and $1$ respectively. This curve can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,\\pi \\le t\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(y+x)\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =((\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2(-{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,dt \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-1+0]-[1-0] \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-77008/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d7c30c2-5d42-5648-ae49-5a0c7ec43233"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77008"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77032/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "40898a22-6920-5a83-aa26-cff3691ec30f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77032/selection/d2d402cd89b594d41bcd11b129436a1a995bb32de4caeae5740c6c84c906bee9" :answer/id #uuid "70abd53a-ac7b-5e14-8b9c-688a2f63c36d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77032/selection/10374d14a280ecc275ec68a3171160e6daa731692f3618d74a38301d96d99c73" :answer/id #uuid "a441d62a-dd57-5be0-9906-7cbcea70660e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi -12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77032/selection/8dbe1b1f3d971e555d91ba21c91f7211f211eb8875b16bf42c40560c8c48e377" :answer/id #uuid "9c4280de-c493-5a13-bbce-e7d8a242c365" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77032/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "f5a477cc-69e4-5469-b8db-19bbe69f353f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77032/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b92ea35-3cdf-505b-9c80-09274ed9f682" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77032/selection/d2d402cd89b594d41bcd11b129436a1a995bb32de4caeae5740c6c84c906bee9" :answer-field/choices ["q-77032/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-77032/selection/d2d402cd89b594d41bcd11b129436a1a995bb32de4caeae5740c6c84c906bee9" "q-77032/selection/10374d14a280ecc275ec68a3171160e6daa731692f3618d74a38301d96d99c73" "q-77032/selection/8dbe1b1f3d971e555d91ba21c91f7211f211eb8875b16bf42c40560c8c48e377" "q-77032/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77032" :question/id #uuid "04f1da30-9079-5727-a65a-17c34fc10145" :question/math-academy-id "q-77032" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069622/assets/08c3195e7325d853f61562b1f62460cb0796f14377286228f2b7cd40983202ac.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=3\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16$  traversed from the point $A(4,0)$ to the point $B(0,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize a circle of radius $4$ centered at the origin. It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =3\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =3\\,i+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(3\\,i+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)\\,dt \\\\  & =[12\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(12+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-77032/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d7c30c2-5d42-5648-ae49-5a0c7ec43233"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77032"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125047/selection/127c49c593c8e7c961cff2730e901366754130d9efc5f5103fb9901d09c9ff2f" :answer/id #uuid "2790fdbf-9539-5028-88d3-888079a9cf3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125047/selection/0ef9205d1d94b5f102c925d90c61c7fad413c1de70799054eb487de8b12bb631" :answer/id #uuid "9f9e1606-58a8-557c-a6e3-49f73c5ac643" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t)+6\\sqrt{6}t\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125047/selection/2c60184edf0e2cc3b1da8d67d85d1eafea63f76156d7c9ae6106179525ca28b5" :answer/id #uuid "c9f8ed32-ffa6-55b3-997a-c24b86aeca91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+6\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125047/selection/0b23274082e6058e531380cd484bf6f8607e861c5bc3f3270792e1e98b40eb95" :answer/id #uuid "bfb0d7ea-99d3-50ad-afe3-952dc466428f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125047/selection/522934621cb8f52a6c282daf0e485768bac35eb2fcfa0ba86bdfe60a1e3f66bf" :answer/id #uuid "d6c931df-1f47-523e-80a7-96ae3668f44f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t)+3\\sqrt{6}t\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125047/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "53fd0561-0984-5a0c-9670-b6fbf2e18e94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125047/selection/127c49c593c8e7c961cff2730e901366754130d9efc5f5103fb9901d09c9ff2f" :answer-field/choices ["q-125047/selection/127c49c593c8e7c961cff2730e901366754130d9efc5f5103fb9901d09c9ff2f" "q-125047/selection/0ef9205d1d94b5f102c925d90c61c7fad413c1de70799054eb487de8b12bb631" "q-125047/selection/2c60184edf0e2cc3b1da8d67d85d1eafea63f76156d7c9ae6106179525ca28b5" "q-125047/selection/0b23274082e6058e531380cd484bf6f8607e861c5bc3f3270792e1e98b40eb95" "q-125047/selection/522934621cb8f52a6c282daf0e485768bac35eb2fcfa0ba86bdfe60a1e3f66bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125047" :question/id #uuid "4b9560c5-3975-50c2-be49-907f5e986e32" :question/math-academy-id "q-125047" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\sqrt{xy}\\,j$ and $C$ is the line segment traversed from the point $A(1,1)$ to the point $B(4,3)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(1+3t)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the line segment.\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are \n$a=i+j$ and $b=4\\,i+3\\,j.$\nSo, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =(i+j)+t[(4\\,i+3\\,j)-(i+j)] \\\\  & =(i+j)+t(3i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =(1+3t)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ varies from $t=0$ (at the point $A$) to $t=1$ (at the point $B$).\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=1+3t,\\,y=1+2t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,i+\\sqrt{xy}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3t+1+2t)\\,i+\\sqrt{(1+3t)(1+2t)}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,j)\\cdot (3\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)\\cdot 3+\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+5t)+2\\sqrt{1+5t+6{t}^{2}}\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125047/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0983e1e6-46a9-53de-83f5-a28d5b1eee47"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125047"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125065/selection/5cc7b099250874d5d241aaa6b3721e890db72d33245143a0fa2adc48f5ac0e61" :answer/id #uuid "ed46e1fc-ec22-5349-8a9c-98856b673a11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125065/selection/6a98c6f6b9de354c5354d19c87234120cb88a73f82841824bea259af0af81706" :answer/id #uuid "c8ee05bc-92ff-58be-9189-349e4480ad7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125065/selection/ff8166472d9a4dfeb5495587173d3a2d621c08d3e652dd0de69dfe56124839f3" :answer/id #uuid "06237856-dba3-5602-a1ea-9cb2e60c7ec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125065/selection/8cab1c9796b75da60c659bae725bb7a4825c9cbfd9ed307b84c5c515c3fffafa" :answer/id #uuid "7bd3f11d-30ad-53f8-8d47-b51f76d658f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e-1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125065/selection/5a10801a8f42b864cc73d99959e35b6190c75accdd832d98b81dc735db730bd4" :answer/id #uuid "4678d7e5-82b8-5e87-9c6b-b5dfd48f83e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125065/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef7f9e25-d9ec-5d72-885f-ed71ee3ac6b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125065/selection/ff8166472d9a4dfeb5495587173d3a2d621c08d3e652dd0de69dfe56124839f3" :answer-field/choices ["q-125065/selection/5cc7b099250874d5d241aaa6b3721e890db72d33245143a0fa2adc48f5ac0e61" "q-125065/selection/6a98c6f6b9de354c5354d19c87234120cb88a73f82841824bea259af0af81706" "q-125065/selection/ff8166472d9a4dfeb5495587173d3a2d621c08d3e652dd0de69dfe56124839f3" "q-125065/selection/8cab1c9796b75da60c659bae725bb7a4825c9cbfd9ed307b84c5c515c3fffafa" "q-125065/selection/5a10801a8f42b864cc73d99959e35b6190c75accdd832d98b81dc735db730bd4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125065" :question/id #uuid "93eab229-7847-5466-9349-e69354e42020" :question/math-academy-id "q-125065" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i+2y\\,j$ and $C$ is the curve $\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-x=0$ traversed from the point $A(0,1)$ to the point $B(1,e).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Making $x$ the subject of the equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-x=0\\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.\n$$\n\nSo, the parametrization of the curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j,\\,1\\le t\\le e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+2y\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+2t\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+2t\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}+2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡t}{2}+{t}^{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}+{e}^{2})-(0+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-125065/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6eddefb-d4b9-5e5b-9278-94de0d8dbff6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125065"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125119/selection/ed831fbcb8cf739efefabb9ad860c979463900ac79997b5e29efc93f784e8c28" :answer/id #uuid "a436f2bb-1a72-5a83-a377-98dfba9a9f4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-5\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125119/selection/436d91be61191a995536ebb6c45d091f8a8446150833554d4cc1b9455fb48520" :answer/id #uuid "f63f7263-d177-53f7-b86d-89ddbfcd5fbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t+6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125119/selection/72faa18fb15e9beaaa67737292a2d9223ba653113bf27e9b333fd33db1c76d3f" :answer/id #uuid "4cc3892f-9f03-50d7-b490-58aeb2789c71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t+5\\sqrt{t}+3)\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125119/selection/f6e9786efce2ea19c80bf58332e78c2c7ef2f37c9fa1c5ee72e27fda15da244f" :answer/id #uuid "a8ae2d93-ee15-5bd6-948f-30d522d0fad2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125119/selection/a7e621f4d59c794c1ddad6dacafd97cdeda1866b390a41b86e3fa58481f7a96f" :answer/id #uuid "1658e889-2720-538f-91da-00561f458388" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-4\\sqrt{t}+3)\\,dt" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125119/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "09db5dcb-67ae-5125-ba36-290effd28794" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125119/selection/ed831fbcb8cf739efefabb9ad860c979463900ac79997b5e29efc93f784e8c28" :answer-field/choices ["q-125119/selection/ed831fbcb8cf739efefabb9ad860c979463900ac79997b5e29efc93f784e8c28" "q-125119/selection/436d91be61191a995536ebb6c45d091f8a8446150833554d4cc1b9455fb48520" "q-125119/selection/72faa18fb15e9beaaa67737292a2d9223ba653113bf27e9b333fd33db1c76d3f" "q-125119/selection/f6e9786efce2ea19c80bf58332e78c2c7ef2f37c9fa1c5ee72e27fda15da244f" "q-125119/selection/a7e621f4d59c794c1ddad6dacafd97cdeda1866b390a41b86e3fa58481f7a96f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125119" :question/id #uuid "df07dcc3-786b-5aae-b240-3c57fcb3d038" :question/math-academy-id "q-125119" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=2y\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j$ and $C$ is the curve $\\sqrt{y}=x+3$ traversed from the point $A(-3,0)$ to the point $B(-1,4)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=(\\sqrt{t}-3)\\,i+t\\,j.$*" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. This is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(\\sqrt{t}-3)\\,i+t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{t}-3,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2t\\,i+(\\sqrt{t}-3)^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+(t-6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}-3)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2t\\,i+(t-6\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =2t\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+t-6\\sqrt{t}+9 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{t}+t-6\\sqrt{t}+9 \\\\  & =t-5\\sqrt{t}+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(t-5\\sqrt{t}+9)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125119/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6eddefb-d4b9-5e5b-9278-94de0d8dbff6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
